    title: "Postwar Poverty and Lung Disease",
    body: "After the war ended, Japan was a field of ashes. Otaki was no exception: he had to survive amid food shortages and poverty. He dreamed of becoming a performer, but the reality of barely being able to eat stood in his way.\n\nWhat made things worse was a lung disease. Malnutrition and harsh conditions ravaged his body, leaving him unable to move properly for extended periods. Standing on a stage as a performer was out of the question -- mere survival took everything he had.\n\n\"When you hit rock bottom, your true self shows its face.\" Otaki would say this later, but at the time, he had no such composure. He simply crawled through each day, staying alive. The long, fruitless apprentice years were dark and lonely.",
    year_label: "1940s~1950s",
