    id: "sc-249", athlete_id: "otaki", order: 4, stage: "awakening",
    title: "A Late Bloom -- Overwhelming Presence",
    body: "As the years accumulated, an uncanny gravity settled into Otaki's performances. A \"thickness of lived experience\" that youth could never possess began to seep from every word he spoke.\n\nThe turning point came late. Film and television roles increased, and the industry began to recognize his presence. There was nothing flashy about him. But the instant Otaki appeared on screen, the atmosphere shifted. That power of \"stillness\" was something no other great actor could replicate.\n\n\"The true path is to keep crawling forward, one step at a time.\" War, poverty, illness, and decades of thankless apprenticeship. Only someone who had endured all of it could reach this summit.\n\nFellow theater professionals were unanimous: \"When Otaki is on stage, the entire production changes.\" A presence that transcended words. It was a radiance polished by decades of suffering -- one of a kind.",
