    title: "Seisha Hicchu -- An Athlete of the Spirit",
    body: "In his later years, Hideharu Otaki commanded the stage as one of Japan's preeminent actors, radiating an overwhelming presence. In television dramas, films, and theater alike, every scene he appeared in carried a weight all its own.\n\n\"He was an athlete of the spirit, transcending words. His very existence was a symbol of Japan's rebirth.\" Those words from industry insiders were a tribute to Otaki's entire life.\n\nLike the kyudo archer's \"seisha hicchu,\" he poured his whole being into every role. He stripped away the superfluous and left only the essential. Having survived war, overcome poverty, conquered illness, and endured decades of obscurity, the man who finally reached his destined place bloomed the most beautiful flower of all.\n\nHideharu Otaki's story goes beyond \"sports\" -- it is a story of \"life's resurrection.\" Not an athlete of the body, but an athlete of the spirit, he lived a life of \"seisha hicchu.\" Crawling forward, always forward, the light that illuminated Japanese culture awaited at the end of that road. He passed away at 87. The late-blooming giant tree kept its leaves green until the very last.",
